poses base/mask or disables."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::guest_force_mtrr_state","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::mtrr_copy_map","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::generic_rebuild_map","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::mtrr_save_fixed_ranges","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_file_add","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::FILE_FCOUNT"],"text":"Guest override is one-shot pre-init under hypervisor, freezing capability. Copy allocates under mutex; rebuild re-adds variables. File add uses per-register counts."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::types_compatible","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_check","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::have_wrcomb","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_del_page","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_file_del","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_write","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_ioctl","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::arch_phys_wc_add","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::MTRR_TO_PHYS_WC_OFFSET","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::arch_phys_wc_del","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::arch_phys_wc_index"],"text":"Compatible if uncacheable or writethrough with writeback. Byte inputs need page multiples. Delete decrements use and clears at zero. Text/ioctl normalize units; combining bias is 1000."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::nmi_perfctr_msr_to_bit","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::nmi_evntsel_msr_to_bit","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::reserve_perfctr_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::release_perfctr_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::reserve_evntsel_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::release_evntsel_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::NMI_MAX_COUNTER_BITS"],"text":"MSR to bit is vendor and family specific. Beyond-max indices succeed without state; otherwise atomic set acquires and clear releases."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_save","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_restore","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_register_syscore","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_value.alt_1","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_value.alt_2","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_open","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_if_init","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_close","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_init_finalize","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::changed_by_mtrr_cleanup"],"text":"Suspend captures ranges, resume rewrites non-empty. Open needs backend, privilege and capability; close drains counts. Late init copies map, warns and registers suspend."}],"locks":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cyrix.c::cyrix_get_arr","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::generic_set_mtrr","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::mtrr_copy_map","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_add_page","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::generic_get_mtrr"],"text":"Cyrix and generic programming run IRQ-saved with cache toggling. Copy and add take MTRR mutex; add also holds hotplug lock and pins CPU."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_del_page","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_mutex","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::set_mtrr","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_rendezvous_handler","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::reserve_perfctr_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::release_perfctr_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::reserve_evntsel_nmi","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/perfctr-watchdog.c::release_evntsel_nmi"],"text":"Delete holds hotplug plus mutex. Programming rendezvous on all CPUs then rebuilds map. Counter bitmaps use atomic set and plain clear."}],"pass":1,"phase_map":[{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p14","crown":"A","phase":"F0"},{"anchor":"HB-KPAPER-001/hb-s5.p04","crown":"A","phase":"F2"}],"schema":"lx.dossier.v1","state_machines":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/e820.c::__e820__range_update","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cyrix.c::prepare_set","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cyrix.c::post_set","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cyrix.c::ccr3","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cyrix.c::cr4"],"text":"Firmware update retypes, splits enclosing and slices partial overlaps. Cyrix prologue saves CR4, disables caches and enables mapping; epilogue reverses."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_del_page","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_seq_show"],"text":"Slot moves empty to occupied on first use, stays while count positive, returns to empty at zero."}],"structs":[{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cyrix.c::cyrix_mtrr_ops","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::generic_mtrr_ops","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.h::mtrr_ops"],"text":"Cyrix and generic tables expose count plus callbacks; Cyrix has eight registers. Backend vector starts with count then set, get, search, validation and probe."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::set_mtrr_data","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.h::set_mtrr_context","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_value.alt_1","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_value.alt_2","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_syscore_ops","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/legacy.c::mtrr_syscore","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/if.c::mtrr_proc_ops","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::num_var_ranges","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_usage_table","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_mutex","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/mtrr.c::mtrr_if"],"text":"Request carries base, length, selector and type; context saves flags, CR4, defaults and control. Snapshot, syscore, proc ops and globals hold count, usage, mutex and vector."},{"sids":["arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cleanup.c::var_mtrr_range_state","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cleanup.c::var_mtrr_state","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/cleanup.c::mtrr_cleanup_result","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::fixed_range_block","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::fixed_range_blocks","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/generic.c::cache_map","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/centaur.c::anon_1","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/centaur.c::centaur_mcr","arch/x86/kernel/cpu/mtrr/centaur.c::centaur_mcr_reserved","arch/x8